SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Giatrissa\, Komia
LOCATION:Komia\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Komia celebrates the nine-day (Enniamera) of the Panagia at the chapel of Panagia Giatrissa — 'the Healer' — with vespers and a panigiri in the churchyard on the evening of 22 August. It is one of the island's older rural feasts and draws Milians from every village\; the same evening the Panagia chapels at Kipos and Trypiti also celebrate\, so ask locals which one has the band that year.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#komia-panigiri-of-panagia-giatrissa-komia
